{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "Fighting the Competition", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "The SWOT Analysis", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 8, "type": "position"}, {"content": "scholar > Grammar - part 1 > Twins After All", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 9, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.1", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Accurately use important information about people's jobs and places of work in communicative situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations.", "type": "secondary_8"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"content": "engenn6le09ob08re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Writing a SWOT Analysis", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "A SWOT analysis is a popular tool in the business world commonly used to help an organization brainstorm its internal strengths and weaknesses, as well as its external opportunities and threats.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "A SWOT analysis is useful in strategic meetings because it is written in bullet-form and gives a general overview of the company and its market.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When writing a SWOT analysis, the <span class=\"strong\">Present Simple</span> tense is commonly used. A few questions you could ask are:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Internal</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Strengths</span></div><ul><li><span class=\\\"italic\\\">What advantages do we have?</span></li><li><span class=\\\"italic\\\">What makes us better than anyone else?</span></li><li><span class=\\\"italic\\\">What are some of the things our clients/customers say we do well?</span></li></ul>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Weaknesses</span></div><ul><li><span class=\\\"italic\\\">What areas do we need to improve on?</span></li><li><span class=\\\"italic\\\">What are things we need to avoid?</span></li><li><span class=\\\"italic\\\">What areas do our competitors have an advantage in?</span></li></ul>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">External</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Opportunities</span></div><ul><li><span class=\\\"italic\\\">What trends can we take advantage of?</span></li><li><span class=\\\"italic\\\">What is the market missing?</span></li><li><span class=\\\"italic\\\">Can we take advantage of the local market?</span></li></ul>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"><span class=\\\"strong\\\">Threats</span></div><ul><li><span class=\\\"italic\\\">What are the negative aspects in the current market?</span></li><li><span class=\\\"italic\\\">What are our competitors doing?</span></li><li><span class=\\\"italic\\\">Is there a change in consumer taste?</span></li></ul>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Language for Comparing", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "In business, it is common to describe companies or products by talking about particular qualities or features that they have.<br/>It is also common to compare two different companies. When making comparisons, you use <span class=\"strong\">comparative adjectives</span>.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "A comparative adjective is used to compare two people, places, ideas or things.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<ul><li>When comparing two companies that are equal, we use the form <span class=\"italic\">as</span> + <span class=\"italic\">adjective</span> + <span class=\"italic\">as</span>.</li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example:<br/><span class=\"italic\">Our strategy is not as appealing as theirs.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<ul><li>When comparing two companies that are different, we use the form <span class=\"italic\">adjective</span> + <span class=\"italic\">-er than</span>.<br> For two or more syllable adjectives, <span class=\"italic\">more</span>/<span class=\"italic\">less</span> + <span class=\"italic\">adjective</span> + <span class=\"italic\">than</span>.</li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Examples:<br/><span class=\"italic\">We have a stronger marketing record in Latin America than the competition.<br/>Garcia Partners is more familiar with Latin American culture than Polygon.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<ul><li>Some adjectives have irregular comparative forms: <span class=\"italic\">good</span> \u2192 <span class=\"italic\">better</span>; <span class=\"italic\">bad</span> \u2192 <span class=\"italic\">worse</span>.</li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example:<br/><span class=\"italic\">We are better known and better established than Garcia Partners.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<ul><li>Some two-syllable adjectives have more than one comparative form. For example, friendly \u2192 friendlier / more friendly. The most frequent forms, however, are: <span class=\"italic\">cleverer</span>, <span class=\"italic\">easier</span>, <span class=\"italic\">quieter</span>, <span class=\"italic\">simpler</span>; <span class=\"italic\">more likely</span>, <span class=\"italic\">more costly</span>, and <span class=\"italic\">more friendly</span>.</li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<ul><li>Sometimes the comparison is implicit (you compare to something which is understood but not mentioned in the sentence).</li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example:<br/><span class=\"italic\">We need to get a clearer picture of who we are dealing with.</span>", "type": "text"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "personalized", "type": "name"}, {"content": "refers to something that is designed or changed so that it is suitable for a particular company", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We offer personalized service based on our client's business objectives.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le09ob08aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "These are words you use when writing a SWOT analysis.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to determine", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to officially decide something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We need to determine what strategy to use.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le09ob08aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "marketable", "type": "name"}, {"content": "sold easily because people want them", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: They don't think this product will be marketable.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le09ob08aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "price range", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the highest and lowest \u200bprices at which similar \u200bproducts can be \u200bsold", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: If the price range is too high, we won't be able to sell this.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le09ob08aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to strengthen", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to become stronger", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: This project could strengthen Polygon's position in the market.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le09ob08aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "financial loss", "type": "name"}, {"content": "refers to when a business spends more than it earns", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We risk huge financial loss for Farmani and Holly's.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le09ob08aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Brainstorm different companies you know about. Make a list.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Choose one of the companies.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Do some research about this company. Make notes.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Create a SWOT analysis based on this company and the notes you made. Include comparisons.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Proofread your analysis.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Share your SWOT analysis with a partner.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"content": "I write a short SWOT analysis. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write about a company. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I compare two companies using adjectives.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "contents": [{}], "_data": [], "id": 0, "type": "welcome"}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "title": "", "type": "audio", "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"image": "engenn6le09ob08re2img05.jpg", "time": "0", "id": 0, "text": ""}, {"image": "engenn6le09ob08re2img05.jpg", "time": "100", "id": 1, "text": "<span class=\"strong notdialogue\">Strengths</span><br/>\nPolygon has a stronger marketing record in North America than the competition, YouBuye.<br/>\nWe have partnerships with other PR companies as well as a strong marketing team. This gives us a competitive edge.<br/>\nWe are better known and better established than the competition, YouBuye.<br/>\nWe have Miranda Morehouse, Head of Fashion, who has extensive experience in the fashion industry.<br/>\nWe offer personalized service based on our client's business objectives, agreed upon PR goals and budgets.<br/>\nWe have a system in place: set goals, determine strategy, creative power, hone ideas, and, finally, define success."}, {"image": "engenn6le09ob08re2img06.jpg", "time": "46000", "id": 2, "text": "<span class=\"strong notdialogue\">Weaknesses</span><br/>\nWe are less experienced in the Latin American market than YouBuye.<br/>\nWe have eight staff on our workforce, only three of whom speak both Spanish and Portuguese.<br/>\nYouBuye has a larger staff, ten of whom speak Spanish and Portuguese.<br/>\nWe are located further away from Latin America than YouBuye.<br/>\nWe don't have enough information on the market in Latin America. We have to clarify whether customers can actually afford Holly's apparel. The product will not be marketable if its price range is high.<br/>\nWe don't have enough experience with online retail."}, {"image": "engenn6le09ob08re2img02.jpg", "time": "87000", "id": 3, "text": "<span class=\"strong notdialogue\">Opportunities</span><br/>\nThe competition in the fashion industry is fierce; this project could strengthen Polygon's strategic position in the market.<br/>\nWe can get our foot in the door in the Latin American market.<br/>\nBy selling clothes on a large scale in Brazil and Colombia, we might be able to strengthen our professional reputation in Latin America."}, {"image": "engenn6le09ob08re2img04.jpg", "time": "111000", "id": 4, "text": "<span class=\"strong notdialogue\">Threats</span><br/>\nIf YouBuye wins the bid, their strategic position in the market will expand.<br/>\nThe potential for selling this type of apparel to large portions of the market in Brazil and Colombia has not been completely evaluated. If the clothing line does not sell, we risk huge financial loss for Farmani and Holly's.<br/>\nWe have no experience working with Latin America. YouBuye is based in Mexico. Therefore, they are more familiar with the culture."}], "audiosrc": "engenn6le09ob08re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn6le09ob08re2img05.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "id": 1}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "title": "", "type": "video", "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"image": "", "time": "0", "id": 0, "text": "Writing a SWOT Analysis <br><br>SWOT stands for:<br><br>\n</li><li>Strengths <br>\n</li><li>Weaknesses <br>\n</li><li>Opportunities <br>\n</li><li>Threats"}], "video_src": "engenn7le9ob08re3vid01"}, "type": "video"}], "id": 2}], "exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "Vocabulary and Grammar", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Listening", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Writing", "type": "skill"}, {"content": " I can write about jobs and work.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can compare two things or people.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can write a short SWOT analysis.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " What project are you working on?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " Is it personal or professional?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " How do you analyze your work?", "type": "Free Header Item"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}], "type": "group"}, {"content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "allowed_attempts": 2}, "type": "feedback"}, {"content": "Ask your partner:", "type": "free_header_text"}, {"content": "Writing Spot: Let's analyze the Farmani project.", "type": "free_type_text_area"}], "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "id": 0, "img_path": "", "stimuli_ids": [0]}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": " Miranda reads Peter's <span class=\"tool-tip\" id=\"tip_1_0\">SWOT</span> analysis.", "type": "text"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Content", "type": "group_name"}], "type": "group"}, {"content": {"attempt_feedback": [